<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narayanhiti Palace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narayanhiti Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a> was the main residence of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. The present building, designed by the American architect Benjamin Polk, was completed around 1970 on the site of an older palace. On 1 June 2001 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birendra-of-nepal">King Birendra</a> and much of the royal family were killed there by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dipendra-of-nepal">Crown Prince Dipendra</a>. After the abolition of the monarchy in 2008 it became a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narayanhiti-palace.jpg" alt="Narayanhiti Palace" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suraj Belbase · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narayanhiti_Palace_Museum,_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
